window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-1323ad8861010e1b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"meet-dots\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dots\">认识 dots（专属智能体）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> <p><strong>dot 角色</strong> — 选择你的 dot 角色。角色外观交互预览请查看官方原文；本站不加载官网脚本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introducing-o\"></a> <a id=\"what-is-o\"></a></p> <p>你的 dot（专属智能体）会持续运行，帮助你在不同工具和项目之间推进工作。它工作时，你可以继续与它交谈；有了结果或遇到需要你决策的事项，它会主动联系你。</p> <p>dot 由 GPT-6 Astra 驱动，运行在云端，并拥有自己的电脑和浏览器。即使你的电脑关机，你仍可联系它，而它也能继续工作。它可以利用过往对话和你的偏好等相关上下文，开展研究、分析数据、准备文档和构建软件。</p> <p><a id=\"access-to-dots\"></a></p> <p><strong>dots 正逐步向符合条件的账户开放。</strong> 请查看<a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">可用资格与访问权限</a>，了解套餐、地区和工作区要求。</p> <p><a id=\"meet-your-o\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"make-it-your-own\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dot\">打造专属 dot</h2> <p>你可以在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中创建 dot。在手机上，你可以为它命名、自定义外观并连接插件。在桌面应用中，你还可以连接自己的电脑。设置步骤请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7?anchor=create-your-dot\">开始使用</a>。</p> <p>dot 会先向你介绍自己，并根据可用上下文建议它能提供哪些帮助。它逐渐了解你的工作时，你就可以开始与它交谈。</p> <p>为 dot 命名，并选择它的形状、颜色、眼睛、眼镜和配饰。之后随时都可以更改这些设置。</p> <p>dot 初始会使用类似 @yourname-dot 的账号标识。为它命名后，标识也会相应更新；例如，名为 Alfred 的 dot，其标识可能是 @tibo-alfred。</p> <p><a id=\"make-it-yours\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"stay-connected\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"your-dot-wherever-you-are\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"message-or-call-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dot_1\">给 dot 发消息或打电话</h2> <p>你可以在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中创建 dot，并与它交谈。你可以在其中任一设备上开始，然后在另一台设备上继续与同一个 dot 交谈。移动网页版暂不支持。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：在桌面端和移动应用中与同一个 dot 进行 ChatGPT 对话的示意；场地比较过程中又补充了预算限制。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以给 dot 发消息或拨打语音电话，讨论工作、调整优先级或作出决定。在 ChatGPT 的 dot 对话中，选择电话按钮即可开始通话。通话时也可以输入消息。通话结束后，已分派给 dot 的工作仍可继续。</p> <p>无论通过 ChatGPT、Slack、Teams 还是电话联系，你连接的都是同一个 dot。更换交谈渠道不会创建新的 dot，也不会重置它的记忆。消息仍保留在各自的渠道中，但 dot 可以综合利用不同渠道的相关上下文。若要把私人对话中的信息分享给其他人，dot 会先确认你是否允许。</p> <p>告诉 dot 不同类型的更新应发到哪里。例如，可以让它在 ChatGPT 中汇报日常进展，需要作出决定时再通过 Slack 联系你。还要说明哪些变化需要提醒你，例如某个截止日期可能无法按时完成。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-where-o-can-reach-you\"></a> <a id=\"where-to-use-o\"></a></p> <p>打开 dot 的个人资料，选择 <strong>添加（Add）</strong>，即可连接可用的联系方式。渠道详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">给 dot 发消息</a>。</p> <p>在 Slack 中，你可以直接给 dot 发私信，也可以在已添加 dot 的频道中提及它。默认情况下它会回应你；你也可以要求它与其他人互动。它分享信息和执行操作时，仍受现有权限与安全措施约束。请明确告诉它要关注哪些频道和事件；仅将它添加到频道，并不会自动开始监控。你也可以通过 Microsoft Teams 给 dot 发消息。详情请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack-and-teams\">Slack 和 Teams</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-o-works\"></a> <a id=\"how-your-dot-works\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"how-dots-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dots_1\">dots 如何工作</h2> <p>dot 会在你暂时离开对话期间继续工作。它会跟踪进展、判断下一步要做什么，并随着情况变化继续推进。你交代任务后，即使新增信息或调整优先级，也不必从头开始；dot 会带回结果，并在需要你判断时征求意见。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：dot 说明它如何在两次对话之间跟进工作，并在需要作出决定时询问用户。</p> </blockquote> <p>dot 可以自行判断何时暂停、何时重新唤起并继续工作；你不必为每次跟进都设定固定日程。你继续与它交谈时，它也可以让后台智能体并行处理多项工作。它还会研究已连接的信息源，提出有用的后续步骤建议。</p> <p>例如，如果 dot 正在帮你筹备异地团队活动，它可以随着参与者确认而更新人数，并在发送询价以调整报价前先征求你的同意。</p> <p><a id=\"context-that-carries-forward\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"memory-and-context\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">记忆与上下文</h3> <p>dot 会参考当前对话、相关的 ChatGPT 记忆，以及它自行保存的有关你偏好、决定和进行中工作的笔记。这些笔记会在不同对话和联系方式之间延续，因此工作发生变化时，它可以接着此前讨论的内容继续推进。</p> <p>它还可以研究已连接的信息，并保留私密笔记以发现有用的下一步。研究过程是只读的；后续操作仍须具备相应权限。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"where-the-work-happens\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"its-computer-and-yours\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"dot_2\">dot 的电脑与你的电脑</h3> <p>dot 在云端拥有自己的电脑和浏览器，可用于研究、处理文件和运行软件。即使你的设备关机，云端工作也可以继续。你需要查看浏览器或亲自完成某一步时，打开 dot 的电脑并选择 <strong>接管（Take over）</strong>；准备好让 dot 继续后，选择 <strong>交还控制权（Return control）</strong>。连接详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38\">电脑和应用</a>。</p> <figure> <figcaption>dot 的云端浏览器示例：显示加州 DMV 车辆登记续期页面，并带有接管控制权的按钮。</figcaption> <p>{name} 的电脑</p> <p>车辆登记续期</p> <p>dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-registration/vehicle-registration-renewal/</p> <p>{name} 正在控制</p> <p>由你控制</p> <p>交还控制权</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">加州 DMV 网站，显示“在线续期车辆登记”页面以及“开始前须知”清单。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/codex/dots/california-dmv-registration.jpg\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>加州 DMV 网站，显示“在线续期车辆登记”页面以及“开始前须知”清单。 · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/codex/dots/california-dmv-registration.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>接管</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-registration/vehicle-registration-renewal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">示例网站（外部链接）</a></p> <p>以上为官网界面示意，不是本站可操作的电脑或登录表单。</p> </figure> <p>通过 dot 的个人资料连接一次你的电脑，就能让 dot 在工作中使用该电脑上的本地文件、代码和应用。每次只能连接一台个人电脑；任务之间连接会保持有效。要让 dot 使用这台电脑，电脑必须保持联网，并打开 ChatGPT 应用。这项权限与将电脑连接到 Codex 或启用 Work Sync 是彼此独立的。</p> <p>dot 可以使用已为你的账户安装并启用的受支持<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>，并遵守这些插件所连接账户的既有权限。例如，可用 Gmail 查找相关邮件，用 Google Drive 处理文档，用 GitHub 调查代码并准备更改。每个插件都必须已连接，并获准执行你要求的操作。本地技能需要连接一台电脑。连接消息渠道并不会自动授予它访问应用或电脑的权限。</p> <p><a id=\"connections\"></a></p> <p>每种连接的用途各不相同：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>连接方式</th> <th>可以实现的功能</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>消息渠道</td> <td>与 dot 交谈，并在该渠道接收更新。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已连接的应用或插件</td> <td>在相应权限范围内使用该服务的信息和工具。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>本地电脑</td> <td>在电脑可用期间使用其文件、应用并处理相关任务。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>连接消息渠道不会同时连接你的收件箱、其他应用或本地电脑。dot 的云端电脑与你的设备及设备上已登录的浏览器会话相互独立。</p> <p><a id=\"signing-in-to-websites\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">登录网站</h3> <p>dot 使用与 ChatGPT Work 相同的私密浏览器登录流程。网站需要登录时，dot 可以向你发送登录请求。打开请求后，在单独的私密表单中输入凭据并完成所需验证；凭据会直接交给浏览器处理，不会进入对话。你也可以选择 <strong>接管并登录（Take over to sign in）</strong>，自行完成网站上的步骤；完成后选择 <strong>完成（Done）</strong>。</p> <figure> <figcaption>网站登录示意图：Alfred 请求访问已保存的场地方案，随后私密登录表单提供可选的保存凭据和接管浏览器操作。</figcaption> <section> <p><strong>1. 打开登录请求</strong></p> <p>Alfred</p> <p>请登录你的场地账户，以便我查看已保存的方案。</p> </section><section> <p><strong>2. 私密登录</strong></p> <p>登录 venues.example.com</p> <p>venues.example.com</p> <p>请输入登录信息以继续。</p> <p>电子邮箱</p> <p>密码</p> <p>了解更多</p> <p>保存到密码管理器</p> <p>接管并登录</p> <p>暂不</p> <p>登录</p> </section> <p>以上为官网界面示意，不是本站可操作的电脑或登录表单。</p> </figure> <p>云端浏览器有独立会话，与你电脑上的浏览器分开。登录后，dot 可以在后续工作中使用该会话，直到你退出登录或网站要求重新登录。如果提供 <strong>保存到密码管理器（Save to Passwords）</strong>，你可以选择保存登录信息。使用已保存的登录信息发起新的登录时，仍需你确认。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=sign-in-to-a-website\">网站登录</a>。</p> <p>有些网站会屏蔽云端浏览器或要求额外验证。你可以让 dot 改用已连接的电脑尝试。这可能会在该电脑上创建一个单独任务；云端浏览器的会话不会转移过去。</p> <p><a id=\"tasks-and-conversations\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">任务与对话</h3> <p>dot 可以调用后台智能体、开启新的云端线程，也可以在已连接的电脑上创建 Work 或 Codex 任务；它还可以继续处理已有的本地 Codex 任务。对于需要使用你的代码仓库和开发环境的云端编程工作，它可以使用你创建的 Codex 云端环境。</p> <p>云端线程会在桌面、网页和移动应用中显示为独立对话，你可以查看结果并继续下达指示。本地 Codex 任务会显示在已连接的电脑上。任务运行期间，你仍可以继续与 dot 交谈。</p> <p>在桌面应用中，打开 dot 的个人资料并选择 <strong>活动（Activity）</strong>，再打开某项任务查看进度、结果或待你回应的问题。dot 可以检查自己创建的任务结果，并向这些任务发送后续指示。任务运行位置以及继续任务的方法，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p>连接电脑后，dot 可以使用这台电脑处理任务和文件；但这不会让它自动访问所有应用中的每一段对话。</p> <p><a id=\"permissions-and-approvals\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">权限与审批</h3> <p>内置安全措施、你在 ChatGPT 应用中已有的权限，以及自动审批检查从一开始就会生效。某项操作会影响你的账户或分享信息时，系统会检查 dot 是否可以继续、是否需要你批准，或是否必须把这一步交由你亲自完成。</p> <p>你可以补充工作指示，例如要求 dot 先展示草稿、经你确认后再发送。自定义规则是可选的长期约束，可进一步说明更具体的边界。无论是工作指示还是自定义规则，都不能覆盖内置安全要求。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">控制 dot</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-dots-compare-with-chatgpt-work-and-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dots-chatgpt-workcodex\">dots 与 ChatGPT Work、Codex 有何区别</h2> <p>下面说明 dots 与 ChatGPT Work、Codex 的区别，以及它们如何配合工作。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>使用方式</th> <th>适用场景</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>聊天</td> <td>你希望在对话中获得答案、解释、创意，或得到起草内容的帮助。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT Work</td> <td>你有一项要委派的任务，例如研究、分析或创建文件；可以立即执行，也可以按日程安排。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex</td> <td>你希望构建、调试、测试或评审软件，并直接使用代码和开发者工具开展工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>你的 dot</td> <td>你希望智能体持续跟踪一项职责，随情况变化判断下一步，并在两次对话之间继续跟进。它可以通过 ChatGPT、Slack 或 Teams 向你汇报，也可以将任务委派给 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"what-o-can-do\"></a> <a id=\"things-to-try-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"try-more-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"what-could-you-do-with-yours\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"work-with-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dot_3\">与 dot 协同工作</h2> <p>可以先把你经常需要检查或更新的工作交给 dot。说明它负责什么，并提供所需资料；然后查看它的工作成果，指出需要修改的地方。</p> <p><a id=\"work-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"start-working-together\"></a> <a id=\"give-o-your-first-task\"></a> <a id=\"an-event-youre-organizing\"></a> <a id=\"a-project-youre-working-on\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"give-it-a-responsibility\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">交代一项持续职责</h3> <p>例如筹备异地团队活动时，可以分享计划和场地邮件，并让 dot 列出接下来需要作出的决定和即将到来的截止日期。</p> <figure><figcaption>筹备异地团队活动</figcaption><blockquote><p>帮我确保异地团队活动按计划推进。阅读我分享的计划和场地邮件，并列出待作出的决定、截止日期和仍在等待的事项。重点关注任何影响预算或本周需要答复的内容。起草建议回复供我审阅，但不要发送。</p></blockquote></figure> <p>查看第一版结果；在扩大 dot 的职责范围前，先补齐遗漏信息并纠正错误。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-working-together\"></a> <a id=\"things-you-want-to-follow-through-on\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choose-when-and-where-to-hear-from-it\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">选择接收通知的时间和渠道</h3> <p>告诉 dot 哪些内容需要持续更新，以及哪些变化需要提醒你。它可以自行决定何时跟进。如果你希望它在特定时间汇报，请注明时区、持续时长或结束日期，并让它确认日程安排。</p> <figure><figcaption>安排定期跟进</figcaption><blockquote><p>接下来四周，每个工作日美国中部时间上午 9 点检查已连接的规划渠道。事项有变化时更新我们的异地活动清单。如果截止日期有风险，或需要我作出决定，请在 ChatGPT 中给我发消息。日常更新放在清单中。请确认日程安排。</p></blockquote></figure> <p><a id=\"review-and-redirect\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">检查进度并调整方向</h3> <p>优先级发生变化时，告诉 dot 如何调整正在进行的工作。</p> <p>询问 dot 正在处理什么，以及哪些事项需要你提供意见。在桌面应用中打开它的个人资料，使用 <strong>活动（Activity）</strong> 查看已委派的任务。你也可以让它列出重复任务，并确认当前日程安排。</p> <p>使用 <strong>暂停（Pause）</strong> 停止 dot 当前的主要任务。已委派的任务需要在 <strong>活动（Activity）</strong> 中单独停止；重复任务则要在 <strong>已安排（Scheduled）</strong> 中单独取消。结束语音通话不一定会停止已分派的工作。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=stop-work\">停止工作</a>。</p> <p>请核查重要结果及其来源。dot 可能出错；停止任务也不会撤销已经完成的操作。</p> <p><a id=\"ways-to-work-with-your-dot\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"dot_4\">dot 可以帮你处理哪些工作</h3> <p>授予 dot 访问相关信息源的权限，并告诉它需要持续跟踪什么。例如：</p> <ul> <li><strong>持续更新销售方案。</strong> 分享方案和客户要求。席位数量或条款发生变化时，让 dot 更新数字、跟踪尚未完成的安全与技术评审，并整理接下来需要作出的决定。</li> <li><strong>为每次访谈准备内容。</strong> 分享访谈材料和照片，让 dot 起草图片说明、节目简介和短视频片段创意，供你审核。发布前，你还可以用手机调整标题或语气。</li> <li><strong>确保发布材料与产品保持一致。</strong> 连接发布渠道，并分享简报、演示文稿和已批准的视觉素材。让 dot 标出可能影响营销活动的产品变化，并准备修订后的文案、幻灯片和演讲者备注，供你审核。</li> <li><strong>随结果更新研究。</strong> 分享研究资料和新的测量结果，让 dot 更新对比图表、说明重复结果与首批结果的差异，并起草发现摘要和建议开展的后续测试，供你审核。</li> <li><strong>跟进软件反馈。</strong> 连接反馈来源和代码项目，让 dot 调查报告的问题（例如侧边栏中缺少某个项目），并在合并前准备修复方案供代码评审。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">可用资格与访问权限</h2> <p><strong>工作区管理员请注意：</strong> 工作区设置、权限以及安全与治理指引，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">为工作启用 dots</a>。</p> <p>dots 正逐步开放。即使你的套餐符合条件，功能也可能不会立即显示。</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pro 100、Pro 200 和 Pro 500：</strong> 面向 18 岁以上、且不在欧洲经济区、英国和瑞士的用户。</li> <li><strong>Business Premium：</strong> 正在全球逐步开放。</li> <li><strong>Enterprise：</strong> 正在全球逐步开放。dots 默认关闭，必须由工作区管理员启用。</li> </ul> <p>与你的 dot 进行对话不会计入 ChatGPT 使用限额。dot 在 Work 或 Codex 中启动或管理的任务，仍按通常规则计入相应产品的使用限额。你的套餐包含一定额度的深度工作；功能推出后的首月限额会提高。</p> <p>你可以在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中创建 dot。在移动端设置时，请使用最新版移动应用。移动网页版暂不支持。</p> <p><a id=\"reference\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">参考指南</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>指南</th> <th>内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7\">开始使用</a></td> <td>设置、首次对话和分派工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">消息渠道</a></td> <td>ChatGPT、通话、Slack 和 Teams。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">任务与记忆</a></td> <td>已分派工作、重复任务、上下文和主动研究。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38\">电脑和应用</a></td> <td>云端工作、本地访问、插件和网站登录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">控制</a></td> <td>查看活动、管理权限和停止工作。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","en":"<h1 id=\"meet-dots\">Meet dots</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> <p><strong>Dots characters</strong> — Choose your dot character。See the official page for the interactive character preview; official scripts are not loaded locally.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introducing-o\"></a> <a id=\"what-is-o\"></a></p> <p>Your dot is an always-on agent that keeps work moving across your tools and projects. You can keep talking to it while it works, and it reaches out with results or decisions that need you.</p> <p>Powered by GPT-6 Astra, your dot lives in the cloud and has its own computer and browser. You can reach it and it can keep working even when your computer is off. It can research, analyze data, prepare documents, and build software, using relevant context from past conversations and your preferences.</p> <p><a id=\"access-to-dots\"></a></p> <p><strong>Dots are rolling out gradually to eligible accounts.</strong> See <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">availability and access</a> for plan, region, and workspace requirements.</p> <p><a id=\"meet-your-o\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"make-it-your-own\">Make it your own</h2> <p>Create your dot in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. On your phone, you can give it a name, customize its appearance, and connect plugins. In the desktop app, you can also connect your computer. See <a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7?anchor=create-your-dot\">Getting started</a> for setup steps.</p> <p>Your dot introduces itself and uses the context available to it to suggest ways it can help. You can start talking to it while it gets to know your work.</p> <p>Give your dot a name and choose its shape, color, eyes, glasses, and accessories. You can change these anytime.</p> <p>Your dot starts with a handle such as @yourname-dot. Naming it updates the handle, for example, @tibo-alfred for a dot named Alfred.</p> <p><a id=\"make-it-yours\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"stay-connected\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"your-dot-wherever-you-are\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"message-or-call-your-dot\">Message or call your dot</h2> <p>Create and talk to your dot in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. You can start on any of these and continue with the same dot on another device. Mobile web is not supported.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: An illustrative ChatGPT conversation with the same dot on desktop and in the mobile app: a venue comparison gains a budget constraint.</p> </blockquote> <p>You can message your dot or call it to discuss work, change priorities, or make a decision. In ChatGPT, select the phone button in your dot’s conversation to start a call. You can also type messages while you’re talking. Work you’ve assigned can continue after the call ends.</p> <p>You reach the same dot in ChatGPT, Slack, Teams, or a call. Changing where you talk to it doesn’t start a new dot or reset its memory. Messages stay in their respective channels, while your dot can use relevant context across them. Before sharing information from a private conversation with other people, your dot checks that you’ve allowed it.</p> <p>Tell your dot where to send different kinds of updates. For example, ask it to keep routine progress in ChatGPT and bring decisions to you in Slack. Explain which changes need your attention, such as a deadline at risk.</p> <p><a id=\"choose-where-o-can-reach-you\"></a> <a id=\"where-to-use-o\"></a></p> <p>Open your dot's profile and select <strong>Add</strong> to connect an available contact method. See <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">Message your dot</a> for channel details.</p> <p>In Slack, you can DM your dot or mention it in a channel you’ve added it to. By default, it responds to you; you can instruct it to engage with others. Existing permissions and safeguards still apply to what it shares and does. Tell it which channels and events to watch for. Adding it to a channel alone doesn’t start monitoring. You can also message your dot in Microsoft Teams. See <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack-and-teams\">Slack and Teams</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"how-o-works\"></a> <a id=\"how-your-dot-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"how-dots-work\">How dots work</h2> <p>Your dot works between conversations. It tracks progress, works out what needs to happen next, and follows through as things change. Once you’ve asked it to handle something, you can return with new information or priorities without restarting the work. Your dot brings back results and turns to you for decisions that need your judgment.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A dot explains how it follows up between conversations and asks for decisions.</p> </blockquote> <p>Your dot can decide when to pause and wake up to continue work; you don’t need a fixed schedule for every follow-up. It can use background agents to work on several things in parallel while you keep talking to it. It also researches connected information to suggest useful next steps.</p> <p>For example, if your dot is helping organize an offsite, it can update the headcount as people confirm and ask before sending a request for revised pricing.</p> <p><a id=\"context-that-carries-forward\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"memory-and-context\">Memory and context</h3> <p>Your dot draws on the conversation, relevant ChatGPT memory, and its own saved notes about your preferences, decisions, and ongoing work. These notes carry forward across conversations and contact methods, so it can build on what you’ve discussed as your work changes.</p> <p>It can also research connected information and keep private notes to identify useful next steps. That research is read-only; follow-up actions require the applicable permissions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">Tasks and memory</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"where-the-work-happens\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"its-computer-and-yours\">Its computer and yours</h3> <p>Your dot has its own computer and browser in the cloud for research, files, and running software. Cloud work can continue while your devices are off. When you need to inspect the browser or do a step yourself, open its computer and select <strong>Take over</strong>. Select <strong>Return control</strong> when you’re ready for your dot to continue. See <a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38\">computers and apps</a> for connection details.</p> <figure> <figcaption>Example of a dot's cloud browser displaying the California DMV vehicle registration renewal page, with the Take over control.</figcaption> <p>{name}’s Computer</p> <p>Vehicle Registration Renewal</p> <p>dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-registration/vehicle-registration-renewal/</p> <p>{name} has control</p> <p>You have control</p> <p>Return control</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">California DMV website showing Vehicle Registration Online Renewal and the Before You Begin checklist. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/codex/dots/california-dmv-registration.jpg\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>California DMV website showing Vehicle Registration Online Renewal and the Before You Begin checklist. · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/codex/dots/california-dmv-registration.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Take over</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-registration/vehicle-registration-renewal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Example website (external link)</a></p> <p>This is an official-interface illustration, not a working local computer or sign-in form.</p> </figure> <p>Connect your computer once through your dot’s profile to make its local files, code, and apps available for your dot’s work. You can connect only one personal computer at a time. The connection stays in place between tasks. Your computer must be online with the ChatGPT app open for your dot to use it. This permission is separate from connecting your computer to Codex or enabling Work Sync.</p> <p>Your dot can use supported <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> installed and enabled for your account, with their connected accounts and existing permissions. For example, use Gmail to find relevant email, Google Drive to work with documents, and GitHub to investigate code and prepare changes. Each plugin must be connected and permitted to perform the actions you request. Local skills require a connected computer. Connecting a messaging channel doesn’t automatically grant access to your apps or computer.</p> <p><a id=\"connections\"></a></p> <p>Each connection serves a different purpose:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Connection</th> <th>What it enables</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Messaging channel</td> <td>Talk to your dot and receive updates there.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Connected app or plugin</td> <td>Use that service's information and tools within its permissions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Local computer</td> <td>Work with that computer's files, apps, and tasks while it's available.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Connecting a messaging channel doesn't also connect your inbox, other apps, or local computer. Your dot's cloud computer is separate from your devices and their signed-in browser sessions.</p> <h3 id=\"signing-in-to-websites\">Signing in to websites</h3> <p>Your dot uses the same private browser sign-in flow as ChatGPT Work. When a website needs a login, it can send you a sign-in request. Open the request to enter your credentials and any requested verification in a private form. Your credentials go to the browser outside the conversation. You can also select <strong>Take over to sign in</strong> to complete the steps on the website yourself, then select <strong>Done</strong> when you’ve finished.</p> <figure> <figcaption>Two illustrative views of website sign-in: Alfred requests access to a saved venue proposal, then a private sign-in form offers optional saving and browser takeover.</figcaption> <section> <p><strong>1. Open the sign-in request</strong></p> <p>Alfred</p> <p>Sign in to your venue account so I can review the saved proposal.</p> </section><section> <p><strong>2. Sign in privately</strong></p> <p>Sign in to venues.example.com</p> <p>venues.example.com</p> <p>Enter your login details to continue.</p> <p>Email address</p> <p>Password</p> <p>Learn more</p> <p>Save to Passwords</p> <p>Take over to sign in</p> <p>Not now</p> <p>Sign in</p> </section> <p>This is an official-interface illustration, not a working local computer or sign-in form.</p> </figure> <p>The cloud browser has its own sessions, separate from the browser on your computer. Once you sign in, your dot can use that session for later work until you sign out or the website requires another login. When available, <strong>Save to Passwords</strong> lets you optionally save the login. Using a saved login for a new sign-in requires your confirmation. See <a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=sign-in-to-a-website\">website sign-in</a>.</p> <p>Some websites block cloud browsers or require extra verification. You can ask your dot to try a connected computer instead. This may create a separate task on that computer; it doesn’t transfer the cloud browser’s session.</p> <h3 id=\"tasks-and-conversations\">Tasks and conversations</h3> <p>Your dot can use background agents, start new cloud threads, and create Work or Codex tasks on a connected computer. It can also continue existing local Codex tasks. For cloud coding work that needs your repository and setup, it can use a Codex cloud environment you’ve created.</p> <p>Cloud threads appear as separate conversations in the desktop, web, and mobile apps, where you can review results and give further instructions. Local Codex tasks appear on the connected computer. You can keep talking to your dot while these tasks run.</p> <p>In the desktop app, open your dot’s profile and select <strong>Activity</strong>, then open a task to inspect its progress, results, or requests for input. Your dot can check results and send follow-up instructions to tasks it created. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">Tasks and memory</a> for where tasks run and how to continue them.</p> <p>Connecting your computer lets your dot work with its tasks and files. It doesn't give your dot access to every conversation in every app.</p> <h3 id=\"permissions-and-approvals\">Permissions and approvals</h3> <p>Built-in safeguards, your existing ChatGPT app permissions, and automatic approval checks apply from the start. Before an action affects your accounts or shares information, review determines whether your dot can proceed, needs your approval, or must hand a step over to you.</p> <p>You can add instructions for how you want your dot to work, such as asking it to show you drafts before sending them. Custom rules are optional controls for more specific ongoing boundaries. Neither instructions nor custom rules override built-in safety requirements. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">Control your dot</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"how-dots-compare-with-chatgpt-work-and-codex\">How dots compare with ChatGPT Work and Codex</h2> <p>Here's how dots compare with ChatGPT Work and Codex, and how they can work together.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Experience</th> <th>When to use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Chat</td> <td>When you want an answer, an explanation, ideas, or help drafting something in conversation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT Work</td> <td>When you have a task to delegate, such as research, analysis, or creating a file, either now or on a schedule.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex</td> <td>When you want to build, debug, test, or review software and work directly with code and developer tools.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Your dot</td> <td>When you want an agent to keep track of an ongoing responsibility, figure out next steps as things change, and follow up between conversations. It can keep you updated in ChatGPT, Slack, or Teams and delegate tasks to ChatGPT Work or Codex.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"what-o-can-do\"></a> <a id=\"things-to-try-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"try-more-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"what-could-you-do-with-yours\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work-with-your-dot\">Work with your dot</h2> <p>Start with work you regularly need to check or update. Describe the responsibility and share the source material it needs, then review its work and explain what needs to change.</p> <p><a id=\"work-with-o\"></a> <a id=\"start-working-together\"></a> <a id=\"give-o-your-first-task\"></a> <a id=\"an-event-youre-organizing\"></a> <a id=\"a-project-youre-working-on\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"give-it-a-responsibility\">Give it a responsibility</h3> <p>For an offsite, share the plan and venue emails, then ask your dot to identify upcoming decisions and deadlines.</p> <figure><figcaption>An offsite to organize</figcaption><blockquote><p>Help me keep our offsite on track. Read the plan and venue emails I shared, and make a list of decisions, deadlines, and things we're waiting on. Focus on anything that affects the budget or needs an answer this week. Draft suggested replies for my review, but don't send them.</p></blockquote></figure> <p>Review the first result and correct any missing details before expanding the responsibility.</p> <p><a id=\"keep-working-together\"></a> <a id=\"things-you-want-to-follow-through-on\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"choose-when-and-where-to-hear-from-it\">Choose when and where to hear from it</h3> <p>Tell your dot what to keep current and which changes deserve your attention. It can decide when to follow up. If you want an update at a specific time, include a time zone and a duration or end date, and ask it to confirm the schedule.</p> <figure><figcaption>A scheduled check-in</figcaption><blockquote><p>Check the connected planning channel each weekday at 9 AM Central for the next four weeks. Update our offsite list when something changes. Message me in ChatGPT if a deadline is at risk or you need a decision from me. Keep routine updates in the checklist. Confirm the schedule.</p></blockquote></figure> <h3 id=\"review-and-redirect\">Review and redirect</h3> <p>When priorities change, tell your dot what to change in the work already underway.</p> <p>Ask your dot what it's working on and what needs your input. In the desktop app, open its profile and use <strong>Activity</strong> to review delegated tasks. Ask it to list recurring work and confirm what's scheduled.</p> <p>Use <strong>Pause</strong> to stop your dot’s current main task. Stop delegated tasks in <strong>Activity</strong> and cancel recurring tasks in <strong>Scheduled</strong> separately. Ending a voice call doesn’t necessarily stop assigned work. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=stop-work\">Stop work</a>.</p> <p>Review important results and their sources. Your dot can make mistakes, and stopping a task doesn't undo actions it has already completed.</p> <h3 id=\"ways-to-work-with-your-dot\">Ways to work with your dot</h3> <p>Give your dot access to the relevant sources and tell it what to keep track of. For example:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Keep a sales proposal current.</strong> Share the proposal and customer requirements. As the requested seat count or terms change, have your dot update the figures, track outstanding security and technical reviews, and bring you the next decisions.</li> <li><strong>Prepare content from each interview.</strong> Share the interview material and photos. Ask your dot to draft a caption, show notes, and clip ideas for review. You can refine the title or tone from your phone before publishing.</li> <li><strong>Keep launch materials aligned with the product.</strong> Connect the launch channel and share the brief, deck, and approved visuals. Have your dot flag product changes that affect the campaign and prepare revised copy, slides, and speaker notes for your review.</li> <li><strong>Update a study as results arrive.</strong> Share the study and new measurements. Have your dot update the comparison chart, explain where repeat results differ from the first batch, and draft a findings summary and proposed next tests for review.</li> <li><strong>Follow up on software feedback.</strong> Connect the feedback source and code project. Ask your dot to investigate reported problems, such as a missing item in a sidebar, and prepare a fix for code review before merging.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"access\">Access</h2> <p><strong>For workspace admins:</strong> See <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">Set up dots for work</a> for workspace setup, permissions, and security and governance guidance.</p> <p>Dots are rolling out gradually. You may not see dots immediately, even if your plan is eligible.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pro 100, Pro 200, and Pro 500:</strong> For users over 18 outside the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and Switzerland.</li> <li><strong>Business Premium:</strong> Rolling out worldwide.</li> <li><strong>Enterprise:</strong> Rolling out worldwide. Dots are off by default and must be enabled by a workspace administrator.</li> </ul> <p>Conversations with your dot don’t count toward your ChatGPT usage limits. Tasks your dot starts or manages in Work or Codex count toward those products’ usage limits as usual. Your plan includes an allowance for deeper work, with extended limits for the first month after launch.</p> <p>You can create your dot in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. Use the latest version of the mobile app for mobile setup. Mobile web is not supported.</p> <h2 id=\"reference\">Reference</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Guide</th> <th>Covers</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7\">Getting started</a></td> <td>Setup, your first conversation, and assigning work.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">Messaging</a></td> <td>ChatGPT, calls, Slack, and Teams.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">Tasks and memory</a></td> <td>Assigned work, recurring tasks, context, and proactive research.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38\">Computers and apps</a></td> <td>Cloud work, local access, plugins, and website sign-in.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">Controls</a></td> <td>Review activity, manage permissions, and stop work.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>"};
